# Test: ze show host nic returns physical NIC inventory JSON without a daemon
# VALIDATES: offline fallback -- `show host nic` runs the in-process
#            host.DetectNICs when no daemon is reachable, producing a JSON
#            array of physical interfaces with the per-NIC link-speed-mbps
#            and carrier fields sourced from /sys/class/net.
# PREVENTS: regressions where show host nic silently requires a daemon,
#           or where the NIC JSON drops its canonical kebab-case fields.
# PLATFORM: host inventory walks /sys/class/net; the darwin detector
# (nic_other.go) returns ErrUnsupported at build time so the underlying
# feature cannot succeed. Skip on darwin per rules/os-specific-tests.md.
option=skip-os:value=darwin
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp { }
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show host nic
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="link-speed-mbps"
expect=stdout:contains="carrier"
